9"},"performed_via_github_app":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/neovim/neovim/issues/comments/129351839","html_url":"https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/3143#issuecomment-129351839","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/neovim/neovim/issues/3143","id":129351839,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDEyOTM1MTgzOQ==","user":{"login":"Grimy","id":3199732,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxOTk3MzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3199732?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grimy","html_url":"https://github.com/Grimy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grimy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grimy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grimy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grimy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grimy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grimy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grimy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grimy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grimy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2015-08-10T08:06:41Z","updated_at":"2015-08-10T08:06:41Z","body":"You’re right. When the file is first read, `&fileencoding` is automatically detected (based on `&fileencodings`) to be `utf-8`. `set all&` then sets it to its default value, which is empty. Even though the file is not modified by this encoding change, this sets the modified flag. This is surprising behavior, but not actually a bug. It’s also consistent: `:%!sed ''` also sets the modified flag, even though is doesn’t change the file.\n\nA way to fix my use-case would be to change the default value of `&fileencoding` to `utf-8`. This sounds like an overall good change, and it’s consistent with the new default for `&encoding`. Should I open an other ticket for that suggestion?\n","a